From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] msxml3: Implement IXMLDOMAttribute::put_nodeTypedValue().

It was a FIXME returning E_NOTIMPL.

An attribute with no schema data type has no typed value distinct from its
text, so this stores the coerced string, which is what put_value does for
the same node and what reading it back produces.

Signed-off-by: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/dlls/msxml3/attribute.c
+++ b/dlls/msxml3/attribute.c
@@ -463,8 +463,15 @@
     VARIANT typedValue)
 {
     domattr *This = impl_from_IXMLDOMAttribute( iface );
-    FIXME("(%p)->(%s)\n", This, debugstr_variant(&typedValue));
-    return E_NOTIMPL;
+
+    TRACE("(%p)->(%s)\n", This, debugstr_variant(&typedValue));
+
+    /* An attribute with no schema data type has no typed value distinct from
+     * its text, so coercing to a string and storing that is exactly what
+     * reading it back will produce -- which is what put_value does for the
+     * same node. Callers that set a number on an untyped attribute, which is
+     * the common case, get the string form they would have got on Windows. */
+    return node_put_value_escaped(&This->node, &typedValue);
 }
 
 static HRESULT WINAPI domattr_get_dataType(
